[00:13.58]Other sheep Jesus has, and they serve alongside
[00:20.16]those anointed to be Christ’s heavenly bride.
[00:28.66]All the things that are done
[00:31.52]for their comfort and aid
[00:35.36]Are things he considers that must be repaid.
[00:41.60](Chorus)
[00:41.75]“If you comforted them, you comforted me.
[00:44.64]If you did it for them, you did it for me.
[00:47.34]Your labors for them were your labors for me.
[00:50.59]You did it for them; you did it for me.
[00:53.12]If you did it for them, you did it for me.”
[01:31.54]“Yes, you comforted me in my hunger and thirst,
[01:38.34]and whatever my need, you came to me first.”
[01:46.76]“Tell us, when did we do this?”
[01:50.14]these ones will reply.
[01:53.80]The King will then answer them, telling them why:
[02:01.93](Chorus)
[02:02.08]“If you comforted them, you comforted me.
[02:12.22]If you did it for them, you did it for me.
[02:20.80]Your labors for them were your labors for me.
[02:29.46]You did it for them; you did it for me.
[02:37.72]If you did it for them, you did it for me.”
[02:49.68]“You’ve been loyal to me, doing works that are fine,
[02:56.42]as you preach alongside these brothers of mine.”
[03:04.84]So the King will then say
[03:07.54]to the sheep on his right:
[03:11.56]“Inherit the earth and perfection of life.”
[03:21.75](Chorus)
[03:21.90]“If you comforted them, you comforted me.
[03:30.86]If you did it for them, you did it for me.
[03:40.80]Your labors for them were your labors for me.
[03:49.10]You did it for them; you did it for me.
[03:57.54]If you did it for them, you did it for me.”
